{"name":"Lush Life","hex":"#e9f6e0","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"lush","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Juicy, succulent.","Mellow; soft;  easily turned; fertile."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A drunkard, sot, alcoholic.","Intoxicating liquor."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lush"},{"term":"life","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The state of organisms preceding their death, characterized by biological processes such as metabolism and reproduction and distinguishing them from inanimate objects; the state of being alive and living.","The status possessed by any of a number of entities, including animals, plants, fungi, bacteria, and sometimes viruses, which have the properties of replication and metabolism."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To replace components whose operational lifetime has expired."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/life"}],"entries":[{"title":"Lush Life (TV series)","blocks":[{"text":"Lush Life is an American television sitcom that aired between September and November 1996 on Fox. The series stars Karyn Parsons and Lori Petty as roommates who share a studio apartment for financial reasons."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/0/0b/Lush_Life_TV_series.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lush_Life_(TV_series)"},{"title":"Lush Life (Zara Larsson song)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Lush Life\" is a song by Swedish singer and songwriter Zara Larsson. It was released as the lead single from her second studio album So Good (2017) on 5 June 2015 in Sweden, and internationally on 9 June 2015, through TEN Music Group and Epic Records. \"Lush Life\" is an electropop song, which lyrically explores living in the moment and enjoying yourself. The song was met with critical acclaim, with many critics noting its summery sound and catchiness. \"Lush Life\" won a Gaffa Award for Best Swedish Song in 2015, and was nominated for a Swedish Grammis Award in 2016 for Song of the Year."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/8/8f/Zara_Larsson_-_Lush_Life.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lush_Life_(Zara_Larsson_song)"},{"title":"Life","blocks":[{"text":"Life is the capacity in matter, formed of one or more units called cells, for processes such as cell signalling, homeostasis, metabolism, cell growth, adaptation, response to stimuli, and reproduction. All life eventually reaches a state of death. Many philosophical definitions of living systems have been proposed, such as self-organising systems. Defining life is further complicated by viruses, which replicate only in host cells, and the possibility of extraterrestrial life, which could be very different from life on Earth. Life exists all over the Earth in air, water, and soil, with many ecosystems forming the biosphere. Some of these are harsh environments occupied only by extremophiles. The life in a particular ecosystem is called its biota."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a5/Coral_reef..._South_end_of_my_area_%2814119221571%29.jpg/330px-Coral_reef..._South_end_of_my_area_%2814119221571%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Life"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/0/0b/Lush_Life_TV_series.png/250px-Lush_Life_TV_series.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/0/0b/Lush_Life_TV_series.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/0/0b/Lush_Life_TV_series.png/250px-Lush_Life_TV_series.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALush_Life_TV_series.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/8/8f/Zara_Larsson_-_Lush_Life.png/250px-Zara_Larsson_-_Lush_Life.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/8/8f/Zara_Larsson_-_Lush_Life.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/8/8f/Zara_Larsson_-_Lush_Life.png/250px-Zara_Larsson_-_Lush_Life.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AZara_Larsson_-_Lush_Life.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b3/Rihanna_Diamonds_World_Tour_2013_%28Cropped%29.png/500px-Rihanna_Diamonds_World_Tour_2013_%28Cropped%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b3/Rihanna_Diamonds_World_Tour_2013_%28Cropped%29.png/500px-Rihanna_Diamonds_World_Tour_2013_%28Cropped%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"\"Lush Life\" was compared to the earlier works of Barbadian singer Rihanna (pictured).","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARihanna_Diamonds_World_Tour_2013_(Cropped).png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b2/ZaraLarsson_Seattle_NeptuneTheater_17Sept2019.jpg/500px-ZaraLarsson_Seattle_NeptuneTheater_17Sept2019.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b2/ZaraLarsson_Seattle_NeptuneTheater_17Sept2019.jpg/500px-ZaraLarsson_Seattle_NeptuneTheater_17Sept2019.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Larsson performing the song during her Don't Worry Bout Me Tour in 2019.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AZaraLarsson